Interesting idea.  It sounds like you're suggesting that fire resistance
(the normal one) works against mundane fire.  You're okay against lava,
fire traps, and the elemental plane of fire (*natural* effect -- anyone
unprotected might take damage every round), but fireball, wands of fire,
and fire elementals are still a worry.

I could live with that.  If there is a second level of protection that
offers resistance (ignore a certain percentage, or flat amount, or
cumulative amount) of magical fire damage that could work too.  The
intrinsic might protect you against mundane fire, but a =oFireRes
actually *does* offer you more than the intrinsic.  I could see potions
of fire resistance, scrolls or spells of fire resistance, and so on.

